{
  "$schema": "https://appflare.github.io/catalog/schema/v1.json",
  "slug": "cattopic",
  "name": "CattoPic",
  "summary": "A self-hosted image host: upload, tag, and browse images, with WebP and AVIF copies, expiry, and a public random-image API, on R2, D1, KV, Queues, and Cloudflare Images.",
  "tagline": "Upload and organize images on your own image host",
  "homepage": "https://github.com/Yuri-NagaSaki/CattoPic",
  "repo": "Yuri-NagaSaki/CattoPic",
  // The LICENSE file is the GNU GPL version 3 with no "or any later version" grant.
  "license": "GPL-3.0-only",
  "categories": ["files"],
  // The category changed after this release was published: a revision, no new build.
  "revision": 2,
  "authors": [{ "name": "Firefly", "url": "https://catcat.blog", "github": "Yuri-NagaSaki" }],
  "maintainers": ["MendyLanda"],
  "source": { "ref": "v1.0.0", "sha": "7861a5477016717f05e53ea32fe63f5fd74739ca" },
  "install": {
    "tier": "artifact",
    "packageManager": "pnpm",
    // Cloudflare's Vite plugin writes the bundled Worker and its deploy config
    // under dist/ and points wrangler at it; the packer follows that redirect.
    "wranglerConfig": "wrangler.jsonc",
    "workerName": "cattopic",
    // Upstream's build script; the wrangler config has no build.command.
    "buildCommand": "pnpm run build",
    // Worker code that answers at once: 401 without an API key. (/ is the
    // static app, and /api/random answers 404 until there is an image.)
    "healthPath": "/api/images"
  },
  // D1, KV, R2, Queues (10,000 operations a day), one hourly cron trigger,
  // and the Images binding (5,000 unique transformations a month) all have
  // free tiers.
  "plan": "free",
  // Images are stored in an R2 bucket.
  "requires": ["r2"],
  // Upstream has no secrets: API keys are rows in the D1 table api_keys,
  // added by hand (see below).
  "secrets": [],
  "vars": [
    {
      "name": "R2_PUBLIC_URL",
      "label": "Public image URL",
      "help": "The public address of the app's R2 bucket (its r2.dev URL or a custom domain), without a trailing slash. Image links are built from it. The bucket exists only after installing, so leave this empty now and set it afterwards (see the steps after installing).",
      // Replaces upstream's own bucket domain from the wrangler config.
      "default": "",
      "required": false
    }
  ],
  "postInstall": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "**Create an API key.** CattoPic signs in with API keys stored in its D1 database. In the Cloudflare dashboard, open Storage & Databases, D1, the database named `{{workerName}}-db`, then Console, and run:\n\n```sql\nINSERT INTO api_keys (key, created_at) VALUES ('<a long random key>', datetime('now'));\n```\n\nThen open {{workerUrl}} and sign in with that key."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "**Make the images public.** In R2, open the bucket named `{{workerName}}-r2-bucket`, Settings, and turn on its Public Development URL (r2.dev) or connect a custom domain. Enter that address as **Public image URL** in this app's settings. Until then, uploads work but image links do not open. Cloudflare rate-limits r2.dev addresses; use a custom domain for anything beyond testing."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "The random-image API is public: {{workerUrl}}/api/random answers with a redirect to one of your images."
    }
  ],
  "tokenPermissions": []
}
